# Normalize line endings to LF for every text file, regardless of each contributor's local
# `core.autocrlf` setting. Without this, a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` (git's own suggested
# Windows default) checks every file out with CRLF, and a handful of build/test tools in this repo
# parse source with a strict ESM/JS parser (Vite 8's oxc-based transform pipeline) that can
# mis-tokenize a CRLF-terminated block comment right before an `import` statement — this caused a
# real, reproducible `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token` in
# `frontend/scripts/generate-config.test.mjs` on a clean checkout, traced back to exactly this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch line endings, would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
